course: dictionary
lesson: 4617
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. The word high is a good example. «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing» means far up from the ground. «A faster vibration makes a higher sound» means near the top of the notes.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is it about height, amount or sound? In «Some high-paying jobs need long hours», high means a big amount of money, not a tall thing. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
explain: High can also work as different parts of speech. It can describe a noun, as in a high wall, or tell how something happens, as in a bird flies high. Look at the words around it to spot which job it is doing.
fact: High means far up from the ground, or tall, like a high mountain.
fact: High can also mean big in amount or level, like a high price or a high score.
fact: A high sound is near the top of the notes, like a whistle.
fact: «Higher» and «highest» compare things: the highest score is the biggest value in a table or graph.
fact: Read a whole phrase, such as high school or high tide, because its meaning may not be the same as each word alone.
exercise: «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing.» What does high mean here? | Quick and easy | Near the top of the notes | Big in amount | *Far up from the ground
exercise: «A faster vibration makes a higher sound.» What does higher mean here? | Further away | *Nearer the top of the notes, like a whistle | Costing more money | Taller than a wall
exercise: «Some high-paying jobs need long hours.» What does high-paying mean? | *Paying a big amount of money | Needing tall ladders | Paid up high on a shelf | Paid only on Fridays
test: «Please keep the cups on the high shelf, away from little hands.» What does high mean here? | Bright and shiny | Big in amount | *Far up from the ground | Near the top of the notes
test: In a table of scores, which number is the highest: 12, 40 or 7? | *40 | 7 | 12
exam: In «Springboks leap high with stiff legs», what part of speech is high? | *Adverb | Adjective | Noun
